ed for three surveillance periods (calendar years 2020, 2021, and 2022) and compared with visits from calendar year 2019.\"}, {\"loc\": \"text\", \"q\": \"with 95% CIs were examined overall, and by age group (0–14, 15–24, 25–34, 35–64, and ≥65 years) for females and males.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"Percent change in visits per week during each surveillance period was calculated as\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"95% CIs that do not include 1 were considered statistically significant.\"}, {\"loc\": \"note\", \"q\": \"analyses were restricted to facilities with more consistent reporting of more complete data\"}], \"confidence\": \"medium\", \"uncertain_fields\": [\"analytic_depth\"]}", "type": "text"}]}